+        // Turning a panel off waits out its power-down delay (about 200 ms
+        // on an eDP panel) inside the commit, so a blocking commit stalls
+        // the compositor, every other screen with it. Nonblocking, the
+        // kernel waits in its own worker; a commit that would have to wait
+        // behind another on this CRTC is refused as busy, and then waits.
+        let req = req.build()?;
+        let res = match self
